                  "blocks": {}
                },
                "body": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>We work primarily in full-grain leather — the highest grade available, its surface left intact so the natural grain, pores, and markings remain. Our leather comes from tanneries in Italy, France, and Germany, and is a byproduct of the meat industry. Left uncorrected, full-grain leather softens and develops a natural patina with use rather than wearing out.</p><p>Within the collection, specific pieces use specific leathers chosen for the job: grained Togo calf leather for its durability and soft hand feel, smooth goat leather as an interior lining, pebbled calf leather for trays and coasters, and nubuck where a softer, sanded surface is wanted. All are chosen for durability, beauty, and the way they age.</p>",
                    "width": "fit-content",
                    "max_width": "narrow",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
